# Styling

## Stack

- **Tailwind CSS v4** — utility-first
- **Design tokens** as CSS vars in `app/globals.css` (`--gr-brand`, `--gr-ink`, `--gr-bg`, `--gr-surface-*`, `--gr-line`, `--gr-line-strong`, `--gr-brand-glow`, plus shadow/radius vars)
- **CVA** (`class-variance-authority`) for component variants
- **`cn()`** from `@/lib/utils` for merging classes
- **`next-themes`** for light/dark mode (class strategy)

## Tokens, not hex

Use design tokens for any color/surface/border. Examples:

```tsx
className="bg-[var(--gr-brand)] text-[var(--gr-bg)]"
className="border border-[var(--gr-line)]"
className="text-[var(--gr-ink)]"
```

Don't hardcode hex colors. If a token doesn't exist for what you need, add it to `app/globals.css` (light + dark variants) FIRST.

## Variant primitive pattern

See `components/ui/button.tsx`. New primitives:

```tsx
const fooVariants = cva("base classes", {
  variants: {
    variant: { brand: "…", primary: "…", soft: "…" },
    size: { sm: "h-9 px-3.5 text-sm", md: "h-12 px-[18px] text-[15px]", lg: "h-14 px-[22px] text-base" },
  },
  defaultVariants: { variant: "brand", size: "md" },
});
```

- **GoRun variants** for NEW UI: `brand`, `primary`, `soft`, `ghost-gr`
- **Legacy shadcn variants** (`default`, `secondary`, `destructive`, `outline`, `ghost`, `link`) — kept for back-compat only
- **Sizes** are `sm | md | lg` (heights 9 / 12 / 14)

## Dark mode

- Use `next-themes` with class strategy. All `--gr-*` tokens have light + dark variants defined in `app/globals.css`.
- Don't use `dark:` utilities for color — let the token swap handle it.

## Anti-patterns

- Inline `style={{ … }}` for anything that could be a utility or token
- New CSS files outside `app/globals.css`
- Hardcoded colors / spacings
- Skipping `cn()` and string-concatenating classNames
